\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Kept forms compose}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Let the edge weights be strictly positive and the graph
connected. Let #{K} and #{K'} be nonempty sets of vertices
with #{K} contained in #{K'}. For every function #{u} on
#{K}, the \vocabk{kept form}{fdip-00DF} of #{u} equals the
minimum, over functions on #{K'} that extend #{u}, of the
kept form on #{K'}.}

\proof{
\p{\ref{fdip-00DH} supplies a kept form on #{K'} and a unique
energy-minimizing extension of any prescribed values there.
Take a function #{u} on #{K}. Every extension of #{u} to the
whole vertex set restricts to an extension of #{u} to #{K'},
and the inner minimum depends only on that restriction.
Minimizing over the restriction therefore equals minimizing
over all extensions. The common value is the kept form of
#{u}.}

\p{The same completion as in \ref{fdip-00DH} applies to the
quadratic form on #{K'}, once its block off #{K} is positive
definite. If a function on #{K'} vanishes on #{K} and has
kept energy #{0}, its minimizing extension has energy #{0},
hence is constant, hence is #{0}. The block is therefore
positive definite, and the minimum over extensions from
#{K} to #{K'} is attained.}
}
